          "id": "12965697",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Simon, of course you can, but why not set it? Our indexes don't need the atime for any reason.\n\nThe option exists specifically for apps like lucene... see the description from the man page!!!!",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2010-12-01T14:40:00.071+0000",
          "updated": "2010-12-01T14:40:00.071+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12491757/comment/12965700",
          "id": "12965700",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Also simon, i just wanted to say, you need to be root to change the mount option etc.\n\nI think this is totally appropriate for us to do, again quoting from the page:\n\n\"This flag is intended for use by *indexing* or backup programs, where its use can significantly reduce the amount of disk activity.\"\n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
